description:
In crates/transit/src/main.rs (around line 930), the drain match is:

    match drain_result {
        Ok(_) => { info!("ingestion task drained cleanly"); }
        Err(_) => { warn!("ingestion drain timeout, forcing exit"); ... }
    }

drain_result has type Result<Result<(), JoinError>, Elapsed>. If the
ingestion task panics, tokio returns Ok(Err(JoinError::panic(...))),
which matches Ok(_) and is treated as a clean drain. The panic is
silently discarded and the process logs success before exiting.

Fix: match Ok(Ok(())) for clean drain and add Ok(Err(e)) => warn! so
a task panic is visible in logs rather than masquerading as success.
